From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander <4418484+kuscher@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 06:50:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/15] Android: hide what needs desktop folders, windows or
 the network

Open Folder, Open Recent Folder, folder exports and Open in File Explorer
(Android hands out single documents), floating document windows (Qt on
Android draws every window inside the app window), page setup and print (no
Android backend for Qt's print dialogs yet), AI control setup, the update
check (the app has no network access) and script sounds (they run a desktop
audio program). Actions stay registered, as on the web build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/app/main.cpp                     |  4 ++++
 src/ui/main_window_actions_menus.cpp | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++--
 src/ui/main_window_files.cpp         | 12 +++++++++++-
 src/ui/main_window_preferences.cpp   |  4 ++++
 4 files changed, 40 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/app/main.cpp b/src/app/main.cpp
index e727b28..8b381fe 100644
--- a/src/app/main.cpp
+++ b/src/app/main.cpp
@@ -377,6 +377,10 @@ int main(int argc, char* argv[]) {
 #endif
   apply_gui_scale_factor();
 #ifdef Q_OS_ANDROID
+  // Script sound effects play through a desktop audio program (sound_effects.cpp).
+  if (!qEnvironmentVariableIsSet("PATCHY_NO_SOUND")) {
+    qputenv("PATCHY_NO_SOUND", "1");
+  }
   // Keep Patchy's own menu bar. Qt on Android otherwise moves QMenuBar into the
   // Android options menu, which a desktop window doesn't show.
   QCoreApplication::setAttribute(Qt::AA_DontUseNativeMenuBar);
diff --git a/src/ui/main_window_actions_menus.cpp b/src/ui/main_window_actions_menus.cpp
index df96af5..6a8feb7 100644
